The legal texts come from Botswana e-Laws, the consolidated laws of Botswana published for the Attorney General's
Chambers by Blackhall Publishing:

  Botswana e-Laws, https://e-laws.botswanalaws.com (the Constitution page, retrieved 2026-10-28), and the same
  publisher's earlier site https://botswanalaws.com, read from archived copies on the Internet Archive
  (https://web.archive.org), captures of 2019-05-26, 2024-12-04 and 2026-03-23.

The publisher's notice: "Copyright (c) 2026. All right reserved. Government of Botswana."

No licence to republish is given, and whether Botswana's Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Act excludes legislative
texts from copyright has not been verified. This repository is therefore private; whether and how it may be published
is the owner's decision.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per section or schedule, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; amendment and editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left
out; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws the publisher names for each change. The
wording of the law was not changed. Neither the Government of Botswana nor Blackhall Publishing endorses this
repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
